+### 3.1 PHASE B — run after `CHAIN138 END` (22:50:54) under HQ's `LOAD-CLEAR`
+
+One process at a time; `Get-Process llama-server,llama-cli,llama-bench,test-backend-ops` verified
+empty before each launch; every job detached with an in-turn `until`-loop wait. **No perf or bench
+run of any kind.**
+
+| # | Cell | Receipt | Result |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `ninja llama-server` (chain139 serves from `build-vulkan/bin`) | `21-build-server.txt` | **EXIT=0**, `bin\llama-server.exe` linked |
+| 2 | `test-backend-ops test -o GET_ROWS -b Vulkan0` | `30-sweep.txt`, `32-sweep-repeat.txt` | **151/151, OK, rc=0 — twice** |
+| 3 | `test-backend-ops test -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0` | `30-sweep.txt` / `32-sweep-repeat.txt` | run 1 **2126/2128**, run 2 **2127/2128** — see §3.2, NOT clean, and NOT attributable to this diff |
+| 4 | S-X8 27B, `legacy` | `50-cell-legacy.out/.err`, rc=0 | 5 host-split buffers, every one `memtype 1 heap 1 flags={ HostVisible \| HostCoherent } (pref=legacy)` |
+| 5 | S-X8 27B, `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE=3` | `51-cell-memtype3.out/.err`, rc=0 | the same 5 buffers, every one `memtype 3 heap 1 flags={ HostVisible \| HostCoherent \| HostCached } (pref=memtype=3)` |
+| 6 | text identity of cells 4 vs 5 | `54-text-hash.txt` | **IDENTICAL**, sha256 `5fc09c5fded36c61b7365f19af2677487492a33779a2af2d57c92b8dd3be57ff` both arms, 165 bytes |
+| 7 | `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MAX=0` | `52-cell-splitmax0.err`, rc=1 | refuses: *"this model's weights cannot all be placed; failing before any buffer is allocated"* |
+| 8 | Q4_K_XL 27B | `53-cell-q4kxl.out/.err`, rc=0 | loads, **zero** `bounded host split` / `host-split buffer` lines — no split |
+
+**The reorder is proven to have RUN, not merely to have been harmless.** Cells 4 and 5 differ in
+exactly the thing the switch controls — all five host-split buffers move from memory type 1 to
+type 3 — while the generated text is bit-identical. That is the assertion §3 of the previous commit
+asked for, and it closes the one hole an identical-text check alone leaves open (a silent early
+return in `ggml_vk_host_split_prefer()` would also have produced identical text).
+
+**On the `-st` footer:** the two cell outputs differ only in the `[ Prompt: x t/s | Generation: y
+t/s ]` line, which is why the hash is taken over the generated text up to that footer. **Those t/s
+numbers are not a measurement and are quoted nowhere** — single unpaired cells, first-touch
+effects, no control arm. HQ's chain139 produces the measurement.
+
+### 3.2 FINDING — intermittent NaN in the q6_K mat-vec at the 27B lm_head shape
+
+Not caused by this lane, not provable as pre-existing here, and too serious to leave unstated.
+
+| Condition | Result |
+|---|---|
+| full sweep, run 1 (`30-sweep.txt`) | `MUL_MAT(q6_K, m=248320, n=1, k=5120)` **NaN at index 13576**; `MUL_MAT(q5_0, m=248320, n=2, k=5120)` **ERR = 1.000000294**. 2126/2128 |
+| full sweep, run 2 (`32-sweep-repeat.txt`) | the same q6_K case **NaN at index 148360** — *a different element*; q5_0 **OK**. 2127/2128 |
+| that q6_K case alone, 6 consecutive runs (`33-q6k-repeat.txt`) | **12/12 cases OK, 0 FAIL** |
+| that q5_0 case alone (`31-recheck.txt`) | **OK** |
+
+A NaN that reproduces across two independent sweeps **at a different element index each time** and
+never reproduces in isolation is state-dependent, not arithmetic: it needs the accumulated device
+state of a 2128-case sweep on the largest shape in the suite (248320x5120, the 27B `lm_head`).
+
+**Why it is not this diff:** with no `GGML_VK_*` switch set — which is how both sweeps ran — the
+reorder is not entered, `vk_memtype_forced` is `-1` for the life of the process, and the candidate
+walk is byte-for-byte the shipped one. The only added work is one relaxed atomic load per call to
+`ggml_vk_find_memory_properties()`.
+
+**Why it is not proven pre-existing:** no same-source baseline `test-backend-ops` exists — the
+R48i tip engine directory ships `llama-cli`/`llama-server`/`llama-bench` only. **Owed to settle it:
+build `test-backend-ops` at `50b0e9f7f` and run the same full sweep twice.** Until that is done this
+is an open F-class candidate against the fork's q6_K mat-vec path (the tree carries
+`q6_k mat-vec direct-scales` and `q6_k mat-vec activation-hoist+xfold`, both live in these runs),
+**not** a clean bill of health for this commit.
+
+---
+
+### 3.3 Still PENDING, by design
+
+**Every probe number.** The maker runs no perf or bench cell of any kind; HQ's chain139 runs
+`test-backend-ops memtype` quiet (command lines in §2.1) and the served A/B that follows it. Until
+then this lane has proved that the lever exists, that it moves the bytes, and that moving them
+changes no output — not that moving them is faster.
 
